<title>POLAND: POLAND NAMES MINISTER IN CHARGE OF PENSION REFORM.</title>
<headline>POLAND NAMES MINISTER IN CHARGE OF PENSION REFORM.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish prime minister on Tuesday named Jerzy Hausner, his top adviser and a non-party economist, as the minister in charge of reforming the social security system, PAP news agency said.</p>
<p>The post was vacant since the death of Labour Minister Andrzej Baczkowski last November, which has delayed the reform seen as vital for Poland's market reforms.</p>
<p>Hausner will coordinate the work of several cabinet ministries for the reform, which provides for creating new privately managed pension funds and endowing them with shares of firms undergoing privatisation.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
